<main id="content" class="site-main post mt-article"><div class="page-header"><h1 class="entry-title">How Water Features Meet the Changing Tide of Occupant Health and Wellness Preferences</h1></div><div class="page-content"><p class="mt-article-meta"><time datetime="2023-02-07T22:08:00">February 7, 2023</time></p><figure class="mt-article-hero"><img src="/wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4.jpg" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4-100x100.jpg 100w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4.jpg 600w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4-150x140.jpg 150w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4-300x280.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4-380x355.jpg 380w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4-480x448.jpg 480w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4-640x597.jpg 640w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-4.jpg 750w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px" width="750" height="700" alt="How Water Features Meet the Changing Tide of Occupant Health and Wellness Preferences" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure><div class="mt-article-body">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The COVID-19 pandemic has caused a seismic shift in the demand for health and wellness services in commercial real estate. This revolution has already occurred. Prior until now, the main emphasis has been on sustainable building systems, health-conscious dining alternatives, and on-site gyms. But in the current environment, the focus has shifted to improving mental health and reducing viral transmission. A new wave of health-oriented amenities, with outdoor spaces taking center stage, is making its way into properties as developers and office owners adjust to these shifting expectations.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The use of water elements, particularly <a href="/water-displays/">water walls indoor</a> or <a href="/rain-curtains/">rain curtain waterfall</a>, in office environments is one of the newest trends in this field. These elements have several advantages that go beyond just being aesthetically pleasing and fit in with the current concerns of investors and tenants who are health-conscious.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Water Features Add Value to Office Assets</strong></h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These days, outdoor features like ponds, fountains, and rockwork are more than just decorations—they actually increase the value of business buildings. In addition to meeting the increased demand for sustainability, modern water features enhance the aesthetics and curb appeal of buildings. By utilizing non-potable water sources, like rainwater, recycled water, captured HVAC condensate, and grey water, these features not only lessen their negative environmental effects but also appeal to today&#8217;s renters and investors who are environmentally conscious.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Furthermore, the adoption of biological water-sanitizing systems devoid of chemicals highlights the dedication to sustainability even more. Less use of chemicals results in financial savings, less strain on sanitary sewers, and benefits for nearby animals. Water features become a strategic investment by reducing energy and water use, which lowers utility bills and improves the overall appeal of business facilities.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Promoting Holistic Health among Tenants</strong></h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Water features have a significant positive influence on office tenants&#8217; well-being in addition to the obvious financial advantages. Water has been shown via scientific research to have a positive impact on one&#8217;s physical, psychological, emotional, and spiritual well-being. It can also help to create a calm atmosphere that lowers blood pressure and heart rate and reduces stress. A sense of connection to a greater cause is fostered by the tranquil sounds of running water.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Interestingly, well-kept water features are also a useful way to reduce the risk of viral transmission in the current pandemic age. Ensuring the cleanliness and safety of these amenities requires adherence to established health rules and prioritizing filtration and sanitation systems. As such, water features address tenants&#8217; actual health and safety issues in addition to the visual and psychological aspects of wellness.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>A Wide Variety of Options for Tenant Satisfaction</strong></h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These features, which range from the grace of fountains to the peace of ponds and the dynamic appeal of <a href="/water-displays/">interior wall waterfall</a>s, are suitable to a variety of workplace spaces. Water elements can improve a workplace&#8217;s overall design and mood, whether they are added to vast courtyards, modest outdoor meeting places, or even lobby spaces.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Including water features—in particular, interior water walls—is a calculated reaction to changing office tenant needs. Water elements are positioned to be crucial in defining the wellness-focused office spaces of the future since they provide a variety of possibilities for tenant pleasure, provide actual value to office assets, and encourage occupants&#8217; holistic health. The use of water elements stands out as a statement of a progressive and health-conscious approach to commercial real estate development as the live/work/play paradigm continues to change.</p>



